course: dictionary
lesson: 6470
title: Native: belonging to a place
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word native has several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «Kangaroos are native to Australia» means they live there naturally, since long ago, and were not brought in from somewhere else. Ask yourself: is this word about a place, a person, or a language?
explain: «Mandarin Chinese has the most native speakers on Earth.» Here native means the language was learned first, as a baby, so a native speaker is someone for whom it is their first language. «Your native country» means the country where you were born.
explain: Be careful with «Native Americans» and «Native peoples». These words describe the first peoples of the Americas, and they should be used with respect. Many people prefer their own nation's name, such as Lakota or Cherokee, or the word Indigenous.
fact: Native means belonging to a place since long ago, not brought in from somewhere else.
fact: A native of a place is a person who was born there.
fact: Native speaker means the language is your first language, the one you learned as a baby.
fact: Native species naturally live in an area, but introduced or invasive species can harm them.
fact: Many people prefer their own nation's name or the word Indigenous when talking about the first peoples of the Americas.
exercise: «Kiwi birds are native to New Zealand.» What does native to mean here? | *Living naturally in that place since long ago | Very rare and hard to find | Brought in from somewhere else | Born in a hospital
exercise: «Mandarin Chinese has the most native speakers on Earth.» What is a native speaker? | Someone who is learning a language as a teenager | Someone who translates books for a living | A speaker who is very loud | *Someone who learned the language first, as a baby
exercise: Ella says, «My native country is Scotland.» What does native country mean? | A country with no rivers | *The country where you were born | A country you have never seen | A country you are visiting on holiday
test: «After 1492, diseases carried by Europeans killed very many native people of the Americas.» In this sentence, native people means | *The first people who had lived in the Americas for a long time | Europeans who moved to the Americas | People who speak English as a first language | Animals living in the forest
test: «Introduced species can harm native species.» What does native species mean? | Species that have become extinct | *Species that naturally live in an area | Species brought in by people from far away | Species that can fly
exam: Why should we use the word Native with care when talking about the first peoples of the Americas? | Because it is always a rude word | Because it only means a type of plant | *Because many people prefer their own nation's name or the word Indigenous | Because it means the same as foreign
